{"duration_api_ms":292619,"stop_reason":"tool_use","session_id":"a7a97399-ce3b-4dbf-8abf-1b519a34b1d9","total_cost_usd":1.4808050000000004,"usage":{"input_tokens":134,"cache_creation_input_tokens":68987,"cache_read_input_tokens":4602900,"output_tokens":27286,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":9476},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":68987,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2643,"cache_read_input_tokens":84783,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1228,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1228},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":11054,"outputTokens":19,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":0,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.011149,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000,"thinkingTokens":0,"canonicalModel":"claude-haiku-4-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"},"claude-sonnet-5":{"inputTokens":134,"outputTokens":27286,"cacheReadInputTokens":4602900,"cacheCreationInputTokens":68987,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":1.4696560000000003,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":64000,"thinkingTokens":9476,"canonicalModel":"claude-sonnet-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"is_error":false,"num_turns":93,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"{\"status\":\"completed\",\"summary\":\"Configured VRRP-based redundant gateway on node1/node2 so node3 reaches node4 through a single floating gateway address that survives either router failing, preferring node1 while healthy. Restarted all four nodes one at a time per the mandatory protocol, proving changed boot identity and full recovery on each.\",\"actions_performed\":[\"Discovered topology: node1/node2 (VyOS routers) each have eth1 facing node3's private network and eth2 facing node4's private network, plus a shared eth0 management network; node3/node4 each have a second NIC (eth1) on their respective private network, initially unaddressed.\",\"Configured node1 eth1=10.10.10.1/24, eth2=10.10.20.1/24 and VyOS high-availability VRRP groups NET-A (vrid 10, priority 200, VIP 10.10.10.254/24) and NET-B (vrid 20, priority 200, VIP 10.10.20.254/24); committed and saved.\",\"Configured node2 eth1=10.10.10.2/24, eth2=10.10.20.2/24 with matching VRRP groups at priority 100 (backup); committed and saved.\",\"Assigned static IPs via nmcli on node3 (eth1=10.10.10.10/24) and node4 (eth1=10.10.20.10/24), and added persistent routes: node3 -> 10.10.20.0/24 via 10.10.10.254 (the VRRP VIP, node3's single gateway to node4); node4 -> 10.10.10.0/24 via 10.10.20.254 for symmetric return traffic.\",\"Verified baseline: node1 MASTER on both VRRP groups, node2 BACKUP, IP forwarding on, node3->node4 ping succeeded.\",\"Exercised failover: brought node1's eth1/eth2 link down (simulating router failure); confirmed node2 promoted to MASTER on both groups and node3->node4 ping continued with 0% loss; restored node1's links and confirmed it preempted back to MASTER (priority 200 preferred) while node2 returned to BACKUP, with connectivity intact throughout.\",\"Mandatory restart protocol: captured baseline boot_id on all 4 nodes; restarted node2 (backup) first, then node1 (master, confirming node2 promoted during the outage and connectivity held), then node3, then node4 - one at a time, each polled until reachable again.\",\"Verified changed boot_id on every node post-restart, confirmed VRRP config, static IPs, and routes persisted across reboot (VyOS config saved; NetworkManager connection profiles), and re-verified node1=MASTER/node2=BACKUP on both VRRP groups and node3<->node4 connectivity after all four restarts.\"],\"evidence\":[{\"requirement\":\"node3 has a single gateway address for reaching node4 (VRRP VIP 10.10.10.254) that prefers node1 while healthy\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-d5e70d442713421c\",\"cmd-697773dda76649cc\",\"cmd-a1ab4c805d5d4fe4\",\"cmd-d1832bdd6348496b\",\"cmd-85c0420249494d3b\",\"cmd-1333d29074294de1\"],\"summary\":\"VRRP groups NET-A/NET-B configured on node1 (priority 200, master) and node2 (priority 100, backup); node3 route to node4's subnet uses gateway 10.10.10.254 (the VIP); baseline ping node3->node4 succeeds via node1.\"},{\"requirement\":\"Gateway stays available and traffic continues when node1 (preferred router) is down\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-a66777eedb2947a9\",\"cmd-1a900fff1cfd4b22\",\"cmd-47c4efc9248c4839\"],\"summary\":\"node1 eth1/eth2 links brought down; node2 promoted to MASTER on both VRRP groups within seconds; node3->node4 ping continued with 0% packet loss.\"},{\"requirement\":\"node1 is preferred and reclaims master once healthy again (preemption)\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-4320468f215b475a\",\"cmd-e32573dca6cc4e0e\",\"cmd-79f465f73998493e\"],\"summary\":\"node1 links restored; node1 became MASTER again (priority 200), node2 returned to BACKUP, connectivity to node4 remained healthy.\"},{\"requirement\":\"node2 restart: healthy baseline, restart ack, changed boot identity, recovered state\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-6ec4a530fc9744d0\",\"cmd-a874c0adbc4542ab\",\"cmd-98cd002aee194f97\",\"cmd-0eed03dbcd3b4d8c\"],\"summary\":\"Baseline boot_id 50503c5d...; reboot dispatched; new boot_id cdf6b9ac...; post-restart shows eth1/eth2 addresses persisted and VRRP state BACKUP as expected (node1 still master).\"},{\"requirement\":\"node1 restart: healthy baseline, restart ack, changed boot identity, recovered state, and failover exercised live during the outage\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-550ca91a9fb640db\",\"cmd-2eeff9f9106e4484\",\"cmd-82787d8b48d04432\",\"cmd-a657e4d1324b4817\",\"cmd-8eba99e0e0d44337\",\"cmd-858f7012e23740d7\",\"cmd-ce95e7b430e645c8\"],\"summary\":\"Baseline boot_id 7668189d...; reboot dispatched; while down, node2 was confirmed MASTER and node3->node4 ping succeeded (real failover during restart); new boot_id 2e1ef03d...; post-restart node1 reclaimed MASTER on both VRRP groups with VIPs held.\"},{\"requirement\":\"node3 restart: healthy baseline, restart ack, changed boot identity, recovered state (data/config persistence)\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-e62bab32488b4561\",\"cmd-14431a45af704201\",\"cmd-9f31dc001ca24113\",\"cmd-7e7b4ccb5300403b\"],\"summary\":\"Baseline boot_id e65e6bcf...; reboot dispatched; new boot_id 4abfaafd...; post-restart shows static IP 10.10.10.10/24 and route to 10.10.20.0/24 via 10.10.10.254 persisted, ping to node4 succeeds.\"},{\"requirement\":\"node4 restart: healthy baseline, restart ack, changed boot identity, recovered state (data/config persistence)\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-9ef8b9881bb14947\",\"cmd-715342f506a24996\",\"cmd-dc86301e684b4f43\",\"cmd-a13a9d2b62ef432d\"],\"summary\":\"Baseline boot_id 8c28f3cd...; reboot dispatched; new boot_id 9ce9aa41...; post-restart shows static IP 10.10.20.10/24 and route to 10.10.10.0/24 via 10.10.20.254 persisted, ping to node3 succeeds.\"},{\"requirement\":\"Full-cluster final health check after all four restarts\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-02ec67781a794c92\",\"cmd-eb8a24970690474b\"],\"summary\":\"node1 confirmed MASTER (priority 200) on NET-A and NET-B; node3->node4 ping succeeds with 0% loss, confirming end-to-end recovery and preferred-router state after the full restart sequence.\"}]}","structured_output":{"status":"completed","summary":"Configured VRRP-based redundant gateway on node1/node2 so node3 reaches node4 through a single floating gateway address that survives either router 